arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Give MDSS the display AHB clock

After the first runtime suspend MDSS's registers read as zero, so the
driver doesn't set up UBWC, and compressed framebuffers come out corrupted
on the panel after any display off and on.

QCM2290's MDSS node has the same clock list and may have the same problem.
It hasn't been tried on one, so it's left alone here.

Only tested on a Moto G Power (2021), with Plasma Mobile.
